title: Lead to placement to policy to billing
participant S "Sales & Marketing / Processing Team (SPA)"
participant Q "Quotations and placement modules"
participant I "Insurers (e-mail)"
participant C "Client (e-mail link)"
participant P "Policies / receipts services"
participant D "PostgreSQL"
S -> Q: lead (LD-); broker slip (BS-) with the risk details, sent to several insurers
Q -> I: request for quotation through the e-mail outbox (template broker_slip_request)
I --> Q: offers keyed as OFR- (premium, rate, deductibles, share offered) or declines
S -> Q: compare offers; chosen offers become a quotation (QT-) or a placement slip (PS-)
Q -> D: price with the product template and configured tax rates (VAT, DST, LGT); commission from the rate matrix; next_document_number('quote'); audit
Q -> C: quotation e-mailed with an approval link (valid 168 h); client accepts on the public page
S -> Q: placement slip sent to the lead insurer and co-insurers; each confirms (binds) with its reference
note: The steps a product needs are set per product type or line in placement.journey (required, optional or skip). Motor goes straight from quotation to policy; fire, engineering, marine and casualty require a placement slip. Co-insurance participants (one lead, shares total 100%) are held in risk_participants.
S -> Q: issue policy (KYC check: ID, vehicle identifiers for motor)
Q -> P: issuePolicy inside one database transaction (source row locked FOR UPDATE)
P -> D: policy POL-; participants copied; receivable INV- with the insurer due date from the credit terms
P -> D: posting rule policy.issue.broker_billed builds the journal, Dr premium receivable / Cr due to each insurer + commission income
P -> D: collection item for the open bill; commission lines accrued for the referrer chain
P --> S: policy issued; policy schedule and slips printed as PDF with the Company letterhead
